b/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1045 "Points, Lines, Rays, and Segments" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106005 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bd3c7493-58ee-57a8-8d3a-3cd07eb7026e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106833 #edb/ref 1061 40003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106833 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a8029d6-f569-5e02-94f4-a8c43054eba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106833 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106834 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106834 #edb/ref 1061 40094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106834 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "79e005c1-44a4-5a62-80df-af13329c4744" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106834 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106835 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106835 #edb/ref 1061 40242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106835 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0bee6a5d-8341-54c8-b8a6-8740368cff99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106835 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106836 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106836 #edb/ref 1061 40243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106836 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4f3e9956-cbc9-58f4-8ef4-625ad217137b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106836 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106957 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106957 #edb/ref 1061 8689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106957 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5170c6de-909a-58ce-863d-4886baeefb53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106957 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106958 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106958 #edb/ref 1061 8690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106958 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8ecf8f9e-5978-5c97-8a02-ed6688aea1aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106958 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107041 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll discuss some fundamental objects in geometry. The objects we'll discuss are some of the building blocks we use to describe all geometrical objects.\n\nA **point** is an exact location in space. It has no size (i.e., no length, width, or depth), only position. A point is indicated with a dot usually labeled with a capital letter (e.g., $P$, $Q$, $S$, ...), as shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/aceb9052aee93f2d7ef5cfc3f6a9c7ace291e6c9525751a2d826c0fbfa0b36ed.png)\n\nA **line** is a straight object that is infinitely long and has no width. We can think of it as an infinite collection of points, extending infinitely in both directions. A line has no endpoints! \n\nLet's take a look at the following line.\n\n![](images/86/861fbcc84e4e293379616a5e18d9073ecfdf4af5f6d17dece22196d332b62899.png)\n\nA line that passes through the points $P$ and $Q$ is expressed as \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ}.\n$$\n\nWe use the \"$\\longleftrightarrow$\" symbol to denote that the line extends forever in **both** directions. \n\nLines can also be indicated with lowercase letters. For example:\n\n![](images/0a/0a2d566ad6126527f4b1a2b5a992688a668b9ff901c6b7716381521a576a0594.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107041 #edb/ref 1065 2161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107041 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a6361854-d380-59ab-8f5c-a64142f383c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107041 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107135 #edb/ref 1064 "A **ray** is similar to a line but has a starting point and extends infinitely in one direction only. An example of a ray is shown below.\n\n![](images/75/750aef546281b34fef8e9aef61c1260894128138022e971d6c19dfd834cfa1e2.png)\n\nA ray that starts at the point $P$ and passes through a point $Q$ is expressed as \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{PQ}.\n$$\n\nWe use the \"$\\longrightarrow$\" symbol to denote that the line extends forever in **one** direction. Notice that the arrow's tail is above the starting point $P.$\n\nSimilar to lines, rays have no width but are infinite in length." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107135 #edb/ref 1065 6647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107135 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "74865d26-a257-5d2d-a7cd-537189af9954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107135 #edb/ref 1067 "Rays" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107136 #edb/ref 1064 "A **segment** is part of a line bounded by two points, called the **endpoints** of the segment. An example of a segment is shown below.\n\n![](images/6f/6f0d8c12318cc57412be73f2cfb077efa5b06472554e75be41af233c87a9ab17.png)\n\n A segment with endpoints $A$ and $B$ is denoted $\\overline{AB}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107136 #edb/ref 1065 6648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107136 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ee97c2fb-0c77-5af6-b979-587c04a1f0c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107136 #edb/ref 1067 "Segments" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430217 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{―}{RS}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430217 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430217 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0149ea11-3e54-53ee-ba56-7b7961a4c1ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430218 #edb/ref 1080 "images/60/6004e55eda02ca9677c9e681234a9a56af51ed0943a9678f08f42e5635d66bcf.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430218 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/